X86 SB+pmap-noA
(*
 * #350 - control: the PRE-#338 state.  A (pmap_enter) has NO barrier between its
 * PTE store and its cpus_using load; B (set_dirbase) still fences via set_cr3.
 *
 * SB with a fence on only one thread does NOT forbid (0,0) under x86-TSO.
 * Expected verdict: Sometimes  ->  the catastrophe is REACHABLE without A's fence.
 * => the #338 PMAP_TLB_WRITE_BARRIER (P0 side) is NECESSARY.
 *
 * See sb-pmap-both.litmus for the full mapping and modeling notes.
 *)
{ pte=0; cpus=0; }
 P0             | P1             ;
 MOV [pte],$1   | MOV [cpus],$1  ;
                | MFENCE         ;
 MOV EAX,[cpus] | MOV EAX,[pte]  ;
exists (0:EAX=0 /\ 1:EAX=0)
